<body>

<h1>Island Trade Architect: Sustainable Paths</h1>
<p id="subtitle">A simulation tool for exploring how isolated coastal settlements can build fair resource-sharing networks, hold off environmental and physical threats, and stay resilient without stripping the land bare. Draw trade routes, defend your settlements from raiders, wildlife, and invasive species, and pick a role that shapes how you play.</p>

<div id="a11y-bar" role="group" aria-label="Accessibility settings">
  <button id="contrast-toggle" aria-pressed="false">🌓 High Contrast</button>
  <button id="motion-toggle" aria-pressed="false">🐢 Reduce Motion</button>
  <button id="about-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-panel">ℹ️ About This Project</button>
</div>
<div id="about-panel" class="stat-card" style="display:none; max-width:780px; margin-bottom:8px;">
  <h3>Problem &amp; Purpose</h3>
  <p style="font-size:12px; line-height:1.5; margin:0;">
    Small, isolated coastal communities often each hold only one resource in abundance (wood, food, fresh water, or minerals) and can collapse quickly from starvation, overharvesting, raids, or unchecked invasive species if they can't cooperate. This tool models that tension: players design custom trade paths to move surplus resources to clans in need, invest in defenses against outside threats, and manage the health of four distinct habitats. A live <strong>Resource Equity Index</strong> and <strong>Environmental Health</strong> meter show the real cost of over-relying on any single settlement's land, while optional player roles change how you're best able to help.
  </p>
</div>

